OL,2,V55555555CONE-HOUR LONDON TRANSPORT
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CSTRIKE CALLED
OL,5, Union leaders representing London's
OL,6, bus and Tube workers have called for
OL,7, a one-hour stoppage tomorrow over the
OL,8, Government's union ban at GCHQ.
OL,10, The walk-out, between 1pm and 2pm,could
OL,11, mean disruption for up to three hours,
OL,12, but the evening rush should not be hit.
OL,14, Other train and ferry services could
OL,15, also be affected.
OL,17, NUR general secretary Jimmy Knapp has
OL,18, urged members to give "absolute
OL,19, support" wherever possible.
OL,21, But the two main teaching unions - the
OL,22, NUT and NAS/UWT - have decided not to
OL,23, advise their members to strike.
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49610
SC,0010
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1772236666
OL,1,V7w3s7s35                         G10/18
OL,2,V55555555CHOWE DEFENDS
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CUNION BAN AT GCHQ
OL,5, Foreign Secretary Sir Geoffrey Howe has
OL,6, denied claims that the Government's
OL,7, union ban at GCHQ is the first step to
OL,8, a wider action in the Civil Service.
OL,10, He told a Commons debate two-thirds of
OL,11, the staff there had accepted the
OL,12, Government's #1,000 compensation.
OL,14, Sir Geoffrey maintained that the
OL,15, Government's aim was to ensure
OL,16, continuous operation at Cheltenham.
OL,18, Labour's Denis Healey said the union
OL,19, ban had done "immense damage to morale"
OL,20, in all Government services.
OL,22, The whole machinery of Government was
OL,23, seething with discontent, he said.
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49611
SC,0011
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1772236666
OL,1,V7w3s7s35B                        G11/18
OL,2,V55555555CTUC THREAT TO BREAK
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CGOVERNMENT LINKS
OL,5, The TUC is considering breaking off
OL,6, all links with Government bodies
OL,7, because of the GCHQ union ban.
OL,9, The finance and general purposes
OL,10, committee is recommending a boycott
OL,11, of the March meeting of the NEDC and a
OL,12, review of all its Government links.
OL,14, The committee also wants to raise
OL,15, #500,000 by a 5p levy on union members
OL,16, to assist GCHQ staff.
OL,18, TUC general secretary Len Murray says
OL,19, it is not calling for a general strike
OL,20, tomorrow in support of GCHQ staff.
OL,22, But unions were being asked in a
OL,23, "reasoned way" to challenge the ban.
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49612
SC,0012
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1772236666
OL,1,V7w3s7s35                         G12/18
OL,2,V55555555CDAWN RAIDS IN
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CSERIOUS CRIMES PROBE
OL,5, A number of people have been arrested
OL,6, following dawn raids by police on homes
OL,7, in London, Kent and Essex.
OL,9, Kent Police said the arrests related to
OL,10, robbery, aggravated burglary and other
OL,11, serious offences committed over the
OL,12, last two years.
OL,14, The raids, code-named Operation
OL,15, Mermaid, were made by 150 officers of
OL,16, Kent Police and Number Six Regional
OL,17, Crime Squad.
OL,19, They refused to say how many people had
OL,20, been arrested.
OL,22,F]D This ORACLE page is from 27-02-84
